function home(){
 document.body.dataset.page='home';
 app.innerHTML=`
 <section class="hero home-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div class="hero-shell"><div class="hero-content"><span class="eyebrow">WORKPLACE SEXUAL HARASSMENT · POSH GUIDANCE</span><h1 id="hero-title">Know your rights.<br/><em>Organise your inquiry.</em></h1><p>Free POSH guidance for individuals. For Committees: planned tools to hear both sides fairly, connect evidence and build a record you can explain under scrutiny.</p><div class="hero-buttons"><a href="#guidance" class="btn btn-gold">Free guidance <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="#demo" class="btn btn-outline">Inquiry stages <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><a class="hero-business-shortcut" href="#institutional">For Committees: prepare before the next hearing →</a><p class="hero-disclaimer">Educational guidance available now · Professional workspaces planned</p></div><div class="hero-panel home-start-panel" id="journeys" aria-label="Start free guidance"><span class="home-start-eyebrow">START WITH YOUR ROLE</span><h2>What do you need<br/>help with?</h2><a class="start-choice" href="#woman"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><strong>I have a workplace concern</strong><small>Understand your options and prepare a complaint.</small></div><span class="start-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="start-choice" href="#respondent"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><strong>I received a complaint</strong><small>Understand the process and prepare a factual reply.</small></div><span class="start-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="start-choice home-institutional-link" href="#institutional"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><strong>I support a Committee or organisation</strong><small>Explore professional inquiry tools and plans · Planned</small></div><span class="start-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p class="home-start-note">Structured choices. No names or confidential case details requested.</p></div></div></section>
 <div class="assurance-strip home-proof-strip"><div class="wrap assurance-inner"><span>${window.NavigatorFinder.count} complete FAQs</span><span>${window.NavigatorLibrary.caseCount} source-checked judgments</span><span>Free guidance · No account</span><span>Human statutory decisions</span></div></div>
 ${socialProof()}
 <section class="section home-value-section" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow dark">FOR IC / LC & ORGANISATIONS</span><h2 id="approach-title">The hearing ends.<br/>The record still has to speak.</h2></div><p>If a decision is challenged, the record must show more than the conclusion. Who was heard? What material was considered? Why was a finding reached? Our planned tools bring that work together while your Committee remains in control.</p></div><div class="home-value-grid"><article><span class="home-value-number">01 / PROCESS</span><h3>Prepare before the next step.</h3><p>Essential brings notices, replies, hearing dates and attendance into one workflow. A practical starting point when your Committee needs structure without full report automation.</p></article><article><span class="home-value-number">02 / EVIDENCE</span><h3>Give both sides a fair hearing.</h3><p>Neutral prompts and supporting and contrary evidence records help the Committee examine the material without deciding the answer in advance. Professional adds evidence-linked question planning and a full evidence matrix.</p></article><article><span class="home-value-number">03 / REPORTING</span><h3>Make the reasoning traceable.</h3><p>Professional connects the record to a draft report and three readiness reviews. Advanced adds tools for complex proceedings. Choose the depth of support your case needs; the Committee owns every finding.</p></article></div><div class="home-section-action" id="institutional-preview"><a class="btn btn-dark" href="#institutional">Compare professional capabilities →</a><span>See questioning examples, stage safeguards and the scope of each plan.</span></div></div></section>
 ${whyProcedureMatters()}${professionalPreview()}
 <section class="section home-workflow-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="home-section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow dark">THE PROFESSIONAL WORKFLOW · PLANNED</span><h2 id="workflow-title">A fair process.<br/>Visible to both sides.</h2></div><p>Parties may disagree with the outcome. A process that records their opportunity to participate, addresses relevant material and explains the reasons gives them a clearer basis to understand it. That is the standard our planned tools are designed to support.</p></div><ol class="home-workflow"><li><span>01 / PREPARE</span><h3>Start without assumptions</h3><p>Check authority, applicable rules, member conflicts and readiness before proceeding.</p></li><li><span>02 / HEAR</span><h3>Hear before concluding</h3><p>Record notices, replies, participation and procedural directions without presuming guilt or bad faith.</p></li><li><span>03 / CONNECT</span><h3>Test the full picture</h3><p>Connect supporting and contrary material to each allegation, with fair response opportunities.</p></li><li><span>04 / REPORT</span><h3>Explain the decision</h3><p>Record reasons for findings. Professional adds full draft reporting and readiness reviews for human approval.</p></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="#institutional">Find the level of support that fits →</a></div></section>
 <section class="section home-process-section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="works-title"><div class="wrap home-process-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow dark">EXPLORE BEFORE YOU CHOOSE</span><h2 id="works-title">See the process.<br/>Understand the next step.</h2><p>Start with the free nine-stage overview. See the relevant sections and timelines in a full overview or one stage at a time.</p><a href="#demo" class="btn btn-dark">Explore all nine stages →</a><p class="home-process-note">Free educational overview · No case details required</p></div><div class="home-process-preview"><div class="home-preview-label">A LOOK INSIDE THE FREE GUIDE</div><ol><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Complaint submission</strong><small>Understand the filing window and requirements.</small></div></li><li><span>05</span><div><strong>Inquiry and hearings</strong><small>See the procedural framework and inquiry timeline.</small></div></li><li><span>07</span><div><strong>Findings and inquiry report</strong><small>Understand representations and the report stage.</small></div></li></ol><a href="#demo">Open the free stage guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>

 <section class="section home-knowledge-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="wrap home-knowledge-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow dark">ANSWERS WITH A SOURCE</span><h2 id="faq-title">Explore the detail.<br/>Follow the source.</h2><p>Search ${window.NavigatorFinder.count} numbered FAQs across 23 topics, read complete answers, and explore ${window.NavigatorLibrary.caseCount} verified judgments with their legal points and limits.</p><div class="home-knowledge-actions"><a class="btn btn-dark" href="#faq">Browse all ${window.NavigatorFinder.count} FAQs →</a><a class="btn btn-light" href="#faq/cases">Explore judgments</a></div></div><aside class="home-source-panel" id="law"><h3>Start with the statutory text.</h3><p>Educational guidance draws on the POSH Act and applicable rules. Service rules, facts and later case-law treatment still require review.</p><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="${h(E.SOURCES.act.uri)}">POSH Act, 2013 ↗</a><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="${h(E.SOURCES.rules.uri)}">Central POSH Rules, 2013 ↗</a><a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="${h(E.SOURCES.pocso.uri)}">POCSO Act ↗</a></aside></div><div class="wrap home-community-line" id="community-intro"><div><strong>Have a general question?</strong><p>Explore the moderated community. Keep names and confidential case details out of public posts.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="#community">Visit the community →</a></div></section>
 <section class="section-small home-responsibility" id="integrity"><div class="wrap"><details class="home-privacy-details"><summary>Privacy, fairness and responsibility</summary><div class="trust-grid"><article><span class="trust-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◈</span><h3>Local public guidance</h3><p>Answers are kept temporarily in this browser session for the open page. Guidance answers are not sent to the server and are cleared on reload or reset. Community posting and business enquiries are separate online features. Enquiry contact details are stored privately to respond to the request; no analytics tracker is installed.</p></article><article><span class="trust-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⚖</span><h3>Human statutory decisions</h3><p>The platform does not determine culpability, witness credibility, bad faith, competence of the forum or the legal outcome.</p></article><article><span class="trust-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▣</span><h3>Production safeguards pending</h3><p>Authentication, case-data isolation, security review, legal sign-off and controlled storage must be verified before live institutional use.</p></article></div><div class="inline-note light"><strong>Community privacy:</strong> Submitted questions, answers and private reports are stored for moderation in the dedicated community database. Only approved posts are public. Generated aliases are not verified identities or a promise of untraceability; hosting providers may process technical logs. There are no public attachments, private messages or self-edit controls. Use the report action to flag published material or request review/removal. Retention and removal are currently handled manually; automatic deletion is not promised.</div><div class="inline-note light"><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> Section 16 protects sensitive complaint and inquiry information. Do not enter identifiable case details into an unverified public application.</div></details></div></section>
 <section class="closing-cta home-closing"><div class="wrap closing-inner"><div><span class="eyebrow">FOR A BETTER-PREPARED COMMITTEE</span><h2>Before the next hearing,<br/>know what supports your Committee.</h2><p>Walk through the planned questions, evidence records and report tools. Choose the support that fits the proceeding, with a clear scope before any commitment.</p></div><div><a href="#institutional" class="btn btn-gold">Find my inquiry plan →</a><a href="#enquire" class="btn btn-outline">Request a demonstration</a></div></div></section>`;
}

